  <section class="content-section-centered">
    <h2 class="text-section-title">Free State Soil Testing &amp; Cleanup Programs</h2>
    <p class="text-body section-body-prose">
      Under Washington's Model Toxics Control Act (MTCA), the Department of Ecology operates state-funded programs to evaluate and remediate residential topsoil.
    </p>

    <div class="section-grid-static grid-cols-2">
      
      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Evaluation Phase</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Free Residential Yard Sampling</h3>
        </header>

        <div class="calc-field-group">
          <span class="calc-field-label">Program Execution</span>
          <p class="text-body">Homeowners located within designated high-priority service areas can sign up for free professional soil sampling directly through the Department of Ecology or the Tacoma-Pierce County Health Department.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Remediation Phase</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Free Soil Replacement</h3>
        </header>

        <div class="calc-field-group">
          <span class="calc-field-label">Program Execution</span>
          <p class="text-body">If soil testing reveals elevated arsenic (above 100 ppm) or lead (above 500 ppm), the state provides free soil replacement for qualifying yards, removing contaminated topsoil and backfilling with clean dirt and fresh sod.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-divider"></div>

  <section class="content-section-centered">
    <h2 class="text-section-title">Healthy Actions for Daily Yard Living</h2>
    <p class="text-body section-body-prose">
      If you live inside a smelter plume boundary, following these simple daily habits prevents soil ingestion and keeps indoor living spaces clean.
    </p>

    <div class="section-grid-static grid-cols-2">
      
      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Action 01</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Raised Vegetable Gardening</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">Build raised garden beds lined with weed fabric and fill them with fresh topsoil and compost for growing fruits and vegetables safely above ground soil.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Action 02</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Maintain Ground Cover</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">Keep bare dirt covered with healthy lawn grass, wood chips, bark mulch, or gravel. Plume contamination is confined to the top 6 inches of bare earth; covering it prevents dust generation.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Action 03</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Wipe Boots &amp; Pet Paws</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">Place sturdy doormats at all entryways, remove shoes at the door, and wipe pet paws to avoid tracking outdoor soil particles into indoor living spaces.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-bento calc-strategy-card">
        <header class="text-center">
          <div class="text-overline text-accent-alpine">Action 04</div>
          <h3 class="text-widget-title">Wash Fresh Produce</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="text-body">Thoroughly wash homegrown fruits and vegetables with water and a scrub brush before eating to remove any microscopic soil dust clinging to the skin.</p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

